                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d2b8a468-c4ca-30e0-99f1-28961adbe3bd",
                        "entry_id": "edc12763-1274-3601-879a-d4e85aab999c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство по значению прилагательного дальновидный; способность учитывать долгосрочное влияние, предвидеть отдалённые последствия чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "beed8fbd-8708-4a65-ba31-05838d6d4069",
                                "sense_id": "d2b8a468-c4ca-30e0-99f1-28961adbe3bd",
                                "text": "Притом же, может быть, она, по дальновидности своего ума, и предусматривала с материнскою чуткостью искушения и опасности, которые были уделом моего отца."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "08013b9f-bda4-44c9-9dd5-d8bc026042da",
                        "source_entry_id": "edc12763-1274-3601-879a-d4e85aab999c",
                        "source_sense_id": "d2b8a468-c4ca-30e0-99f1-28961adbe3bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "far-sightedness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "far-sightedness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ac6d188-8e1f-383e-91a5-153a81a65611",
                                        "entry_id": "659ae30d-162b-3be3-be98-bf0cd10350dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of farsightedness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb819a2a-2c2e-4ae4-a732-a793ab26dc37",
                                                "sense_id": "1ac6d188-8e1f-383e-91a5-153a81a65611",
                                                "text": "Marc Brunel was a royalist refugee from revolutionary France. He specialised in ideas that were ahead of their time - of which he seems to have had one a week - and he had a gift for making those around him seem churlish and reactionary in comparison to his own far-sightedness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dedcb41a-d0bf-406a-84a4-41be346d393f",
                        "source_entry_id": "edc12763-1274-3601-879a-d4e85aab999c",
                        "source_sense_id": "d2b8a468-c4ca-30e0-99f1-28961adbe3bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "foresight",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foresight",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3a73e97-c4a6-32c2-8e66-fa311e670771",
                                        "entry_id": "e9b90758-4893-33d2-9056-e8e4503d078a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The ability to foresee or prepare wisely for the future."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9aa10e5c-8319-4cfe-8971-e2f4562a70d1",
                                                "sense_id": "b3a73e97-c4a6-32c2-8e66-fa311e670771",
                                                "text": "Having the foresight to prepare an evacuation plan may have saved their lives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30f34a82-12ac-4e27-ae3e-21c89cf02824",
                                                "sense_id": "b3a73e97-c4a6-32c2-8e66-fa311e670771",
                                                "text": "The rugged forhead that with graue foreſight / Welds kingdomes cauſes, & affaires of ſtate; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feb47bc8-fc7a-488b-a071-9874b8bb570c",
                                                "sense_id": "b3a73e97-c4a6-32c2-8e66-fa311e670771",
                                                "text": "In the dead state all is apparently without motion. No agent within indicates design, intelligence, or foresight: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e06d51c-eb96-4a2b-af2d-239b4f3c0cde",
                                                "sense_id": "b3a73e97-c4a6-32c2-8e66-fa311e670771",
                                                "text": "The specifiers of the Freightliner network had the foresight to base the rail journey on carrying ISO containers which are 8ft wide and originally 8ft tall (although now increased to a height of 9ft 6ins), with a variety of lengths."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0317e045-91e9-315c-975a-b89b46c07153",
                                        "entry_id": "e9b90758-4893-33d2-9056-e8e4503d078a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The front sight on a rifle or similar weapon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "471a6268-85b1-35a5-8bca-ff39f54e8366",
                                        "entry_id": "e9b90758-4893-33d2-9056-e8e4503d078a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bearing taken forwards towards a new object."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8e61b72c-b175-4edc-9a15-14014db756b5",
                        "source_entry_id": "edc12763-1274-3601-879a-d4e85aab999c",
                        "source_sense_id": "d2b8a468-c4ca-30e0-99f1-28961adbe3bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "prescience",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "prescience",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87c27c60-1afb-3de7-94c7-966e25670215",
                                        "entry_id": "7cd62e9c-e2bb-39a8-aab5-4cda454683b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Knowledge of events before they take place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f0d1a58-8434-48d1-9bdc-b1c42d958829",
                                                "sense_id": "87c27c60-1afb-3de7-94c7-966e25670215",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: foreknowledge, foresight"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "679bc3d4-3873-42a7-be93-3f882d517e3b",
                                                "sense_id": "87c27c60-1afb-3de7-94c7-966e25670215",
                                                "text": "God's certain prescience of the volitions of moral agents"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f506670c-f461-405d-a6c1-8835ffede5ec",
                                                "sense_id": "87c27c60-1afb-3de7-94c7-966e25670215",
                                                "text": "O thou, who thus the eye hast veil'd,\nThe book of fate so slowly given,\nI thank thee, that thou hast conceal'd\nFrom man the prescience of heaven."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c53d298a-a76e-43c7-9f1b-f4411b1faf68",
                                                "sense_id": "87c27c60-1afb-3de7-94c7-966e25670215",
                                                "text": "With prescience, the Barlows designed them to withstand a third more weight than they would be expected to bear in normal conditions - future proofing the bridge for the weight of trains we see using it today."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed3ef369-4d2e-4acd-b5b6-b6255945ab64",
                        "source_entry_id": "edc12763-1274-3601-879a-d4e85aab999c",
